{title: There’s a Wideness in God’s Mercy}
{artist: Frederick W. Faber / Lizzie S. Tourjée}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: C}
{tempo: 108}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The Hymnbook (Richmond, Virginia: Presbyterian Church in the United States, 1955), # 110)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]There’s a [Dm]wide[G7]ness in God’s [C]mercy,
[F]Like the [G7]wide[C]ness [D7]of the [G7]sea;
[G7]There’s a [C]kindness [G7]in His [C]justice,
[Am]Which is [C]more [G7]than liber[C]ty.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]There is [Dm]wel[G7]come for the [C]sinner,
[F]And more [G7]grac[C]es [D7]for the [G7]good;
[G7]There is [C]mercy [G7]with the [C]Savior;
[Am]There is [C]heal[G7]ing in His [C]blood.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
[C]There is [Dm]plen[G7]tiful re[C]demption
[F]In the [G7]blood [C]that [D7]has been [G7]shed;
[G7]There is [C]joy for [G7]all the [C]members
[Am]In the [C]sor[G7]rows of the [C]Head.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 7}
[C]’Tis not [Dm]all [G7]we owe to [C]Jesus;
[F]It is [G7]some[C]thing [D7]more than [G7]all;
[G7]Greater [C]good be[G7]cause of [C]evil,
[Am]Larger [C]mer[G7]cy through the [C]fall.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 8}
[C]If our [Dm]love [G7]were but more [C]simple,
[F]We should [G7]take [C]Him [D7]at His [G7]word;
[G7]And our [C]lives would [G7]be all [C]sunshine
[Am]In the [C]sweet[G7]ness of our [C]Lord.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 9}
[C]Souls of [Dm]men! [G7]why will ye [C]scatter
[F]Like a [G7]crowd [C]of [D7]frightened [G7]sheep?
[G7]Foolish [C]hearts! why [G7]will ye [C]wander
[Am]From a [C]love [G7]so true and [C]deep?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 10}
[C]It is [Dm]God: [G7]His love looks [C]mighty,
[F]But is [G7]mig[C]htier [D7]than it [G7]seems;
[G7]’Tis our [C]Father: [G7]and His [C]fondness
[Am]Goes far [C]out [G7]beyond our [C]dreams.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 11}
[C]But we [Dm]make [G7]His love too [C]narrow
[F]By false [G7]lim[C]its [D7]of our [G7]own;
[G7]And we [C]magni[G7]fy His [C]strictness
[Am]With a [C]zeal [G7]He will not [C]own.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 12}
[C]Was there [Dm]ev[G7]er kinder [C]shepherd
[F]Half so [G7]gen[C]tle, [D7]half so [G7]sweet,
[G7]As the [C]Savior [G7]who would [C]have us
[Am]Come and [C]ga[G7]ther at His [C]feet?
{end_of_verse}
